    "title": "2025 Rock & Roll Hall of Fame Nominees",
    "text": "• The Rock & Roll Hall of Fame has announced its nominees for the class of 2025.\n• Nominees include Mariah Carey, Oasis, Cyndi Lauper, Billy Idol, Outkast, Phish, The White Stripes, and Joe Cocker.\n• Mariah Carey is nominated for her significant impact on music culture and has won five Grammy Awards.\n• Outkast, a hip-hop duo, is recognized for their influence on the music industry and has six Grammy Awards.\n• Joe Cocker is nominated posthumously for his impact on rock music.\n• Artists become eligible for nomination 25 years after their first commercial recording.\n• The Hall of Fame considers an artist's impact on music culture, influence on other musicians, and the scope of their career when selecting nominees.\n• Maná is the first Spanish-language rock band nominated for the Hall of Fame.\n• Voting will be conducted by an international panel of over 1,200 artists, historians, and music industry professionals.\n• The induction ceremony will take place in Los Angeles in the Fall of 2025, with exact dates and ticket details yet to be announced.",
